  "published": "2026-11-02T12:24:50.397Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "The same patient now maps to the same payload on every call.\n\t\t  - Every generated List carries its own identifier, derived from the patient and the list's title, so a list keeps its identity between calls instead of being minted afresh.\n\t\t  - A resource that reaches the mapper more than once is collapsed to a single bundle entry, keyed on its type and its id.\n\t\t  - Each bundle entry's fullUrl is derived from the resource's type and its id, so two calls for one patient return an identical payload. The type is part of the derivation because a Practitioner and a PractitionerRole deliberately share one logical id.\n\t\t  - No logical id changes for resources read from the mart; they were already stable.\n\t\t  - The mapper processing service no longer takes IIdentifierBroker, as nothing in it mints an identifier any more. The broker and its registrations are unchanged.",
